From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] dlls: export the functions Windows 7's shell imports

Purpose: let Windows 7's explorer.exe and its shell DLLs (explorerframe,
shell32, shlwapi, propsys, profapi, sndvolsso) load and run as the
session's shell.
Windows 7 behavior: these modules import, directly or by delay load,
functions that Windows 7 has and Wine 11 does not export: ntdll
WinSqmAddToStream, WinSqmAddToStreamEx, WinSqmEventEnabled,
WinSqmSetString, ShipAssert and RtlSetEnvironmentVar; user32
CalculatePopupWindowPosition, GhostWindowFromHungWindow,
HungWindowFromGhostWindow, IsSETEnabled and PaintMonitor; kernel32
CheckElevation, CheckElevationEnabled, GetDurationFormat and
WerpNotifyUseStringResource; kernelbase LoadStringByReference; winsta
WinStationIsSessionRemoteable; on 64-bit, oleaut32's NDR64 marshalling
names (BSTR_User*64, LPSAFEARRAY_User*64) and rpcrt4 NdrStubCall3; gdi32
CreateBitmapFromDxSurface.
Wine before: the modules failed to load, or the shell ended at the first
call of a delay-loaded one ("unimplemented function").
Change: the usage data functions drop their data; there is no ghost
window, no elevation and no remote session; CalculatePopupWindowPosition
places the popup at the anchor inside the monitor's work area, flipping it
when it does not fit; GetDurationFormat gives hours:minutes:seconds;
LoadStringByReference loads "@dll,-id" strings with RegLoadMUIString's
loader; the 64-bit NDR64 names are the classic functions. On 64-bit,
WerpNotifyUseStringResource returns 0 without reading its arguments (the
caller passes them in registers and removes them itself); there is no
error reporting. On 64-bit, PaintMonitor draws the wallpaper fitted to
that monitor, as PaintDesktop fits it to the desktop: traces of the
Windows 7 desktop show a monitor, a memory DC and a rectangle in the
desktop's coordinates, such as (0,0)-(1024,728) on a 1024x768 monitor and
(1280,0)-(2560,800) for a second monitor right of a 1280x800 one
(PaintDesktop's body fills a given area for it). gdi32
CreateBitmapFromDxSurface (ReactOS's NtGdiCreateBitmapFromDxSurface
arguments) fails: there is no DirectX shared surface to give. Other
functions without a public signature (WinSqmAddToStreamEx, NdrStubCall3,
and WerpNotifyUseStringResource and PaintMonitor on 32-bit) are stubs. Signatures follow ReactOS's specs and the public documentation.
Evidence: Windows 7 SP1 x64 explorer.exe and its DLLs load (their import
tables are satisfied). shell32 and comctl32 call
WerpNotifyUseStringResource on a shell thread; as a stub the thread ended
in nested exceptions, with the function the thread goes on (it shows its
message box). With a wallpaper set, the desktop thread called the
PaintMonitor stub and ended; with the function the wallpaper shows, on
each monitor (with two monitors, the second one was black when the DC's
coordinates were taken as the monitor's).
Clicking in a folder window and then on the Start button called
CreateBitmapFromDxSurface from explorerframe; as a stub the shell ended
("unimplemented function"); failing, the shell and the window go on.
Scope: new exports only; nothing that Wine already exported changes.
